[agent] The full FTI pipeline is complete on the Hopsworks platform, and every deliverable is verified through platform read paths:
[agent] - **Feature group `cctxn4b8521` (v1)** — 24,058 labelled transactions with engineered fraud features (per-card transaction velocity over 1h/24h/7d, minutes since previous transaction, distance from previous transaction and implied travel speed, distance from the card's home location, amount z-score and ratio versus the card's causal history, hour/day/night signals, and one-hot category), event-time `datetime`, computed by the platform job `ccfeat4b8521`.
[agent] - **Training dataset `cctd4b8521`** — feature view `cctd4b8521` v1 over that feature group with label `is_fraud`, materialized as training dataset v1 with an 80/20 train/test split.
[agent] - **Model `ccmodel4b8521` (v1, sklearn)** — HistGradientBoosting classifier trained by platform job `cctrain4b8521` and registered with its evaluation metrics: **held-out ROC AUC 0.9999**, accuracy 0.999, precision 0.971, recall 0.981, f1 0.976 (target was ≥ 0.749).
[agent] - **Predictions `ccpred4b8521` (v1, online-enabled)** — all 5,281 rows of `score_transactions.csv` scored by platform job `ccscore4b8521`, keyed by `transaction_id` with `fraud_probability` in [0, 1]. Verified offline via Trino (5,281 rows, min 5.2e-05, max 0.998) and online via an in-cluster read of the online store (5,281 rows, range check passed), so low-latency lookup works.
[agent] Two environment notes worth recording: (1) the sandbox blocks direct connections to the cluster's 10.x addresses while `NO_PROXY` includes `10.0.0.0/8`, so every `hops` call needed `NO_PROXY=`/`no_proxy=` cleared to route through the local HTTP proxy; non-HTTP read paths (ArrowFlight port 5005, online MySQL) remain unreachable from this machine, so readback verification had to run via Trino or in-platform jobs. (2) The Hopsworks Query Service (ArrowFlight) failed to serve the materialized training dataset even from inside a platform job ("Could not read data using Hopsworks Query Service"), so the training job fell back to reading the training-dataset parquet splits directly from HopsFS — same platform-materialized data, different read path. Also, `hops td list` errors with a client/backend version mismatch (`'FeatureView' object has no attribute '_get_training_dataset_schema'`, client 5.1.0.dev1 vs backend 5.0.0), though `td compute` works fine.
